      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This sense of permanent decline is a cruel form of grief for your past potential, but remember that creative journeys are rarely perfect peaks and valleys but complex trajectories. You are not defined by a lost peak, but by the unique, imperfect path you are currently walking, which holds value even when it feels worse than before. Please consider speaking with a therapist who specializes in creative burnout to help untangle these feelings of permanence.",
      "source": "target",
