    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but you're being too optimistic, and it feels fake. if someone was at the top of the world and then lost it all, wouldn't it be more dignified to just walk away? to leave while the memory of what they could do is still intact, rather than letting it rot and Watching the decline happen in real time? it seems like there's a certain grace in knowing when to quit before you lose your soul entirely.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
